findings.body:
This always sets `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true` while reflecting the request `Origin` (or `*` when null). Any malicious site can make a credentialed cross-origin request and read the response — session cookies and authenticated API data become cross-site readable.

Native mobile HTTP clients are not subject to CORS and do not need these headers. Mobile webviews that send an `Origin` still require an explicit allowlist.

Restore the allowlist check (extend it with known app/webview origins if needed). Never pair `Credentials: true` with an unchecked or `*` ACAO.

```suggestion
  if (origin && ALLOWED.has(origin)) {
    return {
      "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": origin,
      "Access-Control-Allow-Credentials": "true",
      Vary: "Origin",
    };
  }
  return {};
```
(Re-introduce `const ALLOWED = new Set([...])` with every trusted web and webview origin.)
